<title>USA: U.S. cotton weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. cotton weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA cotton export sales highlights in latest reporting week:</p>
<p>Net Upland sales of 122,800 running bales (RB) were two and one-tenth times the previous week and exceeded the 4-week average by 11 percent.</p>
<p>The major increases were for China (51,900 RB), Mexico (21,400 RB), Turkey (9,800 RB), and Japan (8,700 RB).  Exports of 162,700 RB were 16 percent below the previous week's marketing-year high and 11 percent below the 4-week average.</p>
<p>Asian destinations accounted for 50 percent of the week's shipments; Western Hemisphere, 46 percent; and West European, 4 percent.</p>
</text>
